      "code": "SSC-PRF-0002",
      "title": "Case-insensitive columns slow queries",
      "bucket": "performance_risks",
      "priority": "medium",
      "what_it_is": "A column is defined with a case-insensitive collation, so string comparisons ignore letter case.",
      "why_flagged": "Case-insensitive collation forces Snowflake to normalize text on every comparison, which can slow filters, joins and grouping on high-volume columns.",
      "snowflake_recommendation": "Confirm case-insensitive behavior is actually required. Where it is not, use the default collation; where it is, apply it narrowly (per column, or per comparison via UPPER()/LOWER()) rather than broadly.",
